From 344ab750ba26c991b5ba782424739c05d4221315 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 03:27:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Visual Style Editor and AI style writer

Visual Style Editor (Tools menu, Preferences > Cite): a tree editor for any CSL
style with a schema-driven inspector, undo/redo, XML view, per-change schema
validation, and a live preview. Edits go to a working copy; nothing installed is
changed in place.

Write a Style with AI: sends a style manual and/or example citations to the
Claude API with the user's own key, checks the result against the CSL schema,
asks for fixes (up to two rounds), and opens it in the editor as an unsaved
style. The key is stored in the login manager, encrypted with the OS key store.

Engine, prompt, reply handling and repair loop are pure modules with Node tests
(236 passing). The two windows were exercised only in jsdom; see FORK.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019d3FPTRa39Yf9hbhHFtye7
